      "writtenOn": "2024-12-10T07:55:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, makes sense. That means we would need to exhaustively list all possible combination that needs the reply. I think we should have that in the util function but we apparently don\u0027t.\nTherefore, for the time being I rather make the CL small, just add a MTU check here for the case we absolutely sure won\u0027t harm anything - after all we just want to unclutter a wrong warning.\n\nI haven\u0027t check this, but I think that the GATTS_SendRsp is responsible to check that a pending response is required, so it\u0027s OK to call it excessively for the other cases.\nAdditionally, receiving a write request is a wrong behavior from the client anyway, since we disable the write bit for this characteristic.",
      "parentUuid": "a60ee36d_40e8d93a",
